1845-4a56-5456-a000-eb06d5845200" :question/math-academy-id "q-316621" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-4,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-4))(x-(-4))(x-1) \\\\  & =2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1) & =2({x}^{2}+8x+16)(x-1) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+8{x}^{2}-8x+16x-16) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+8x-16) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316621/field-1" "q-316621/field-2" "q-316621/field-3" "q-316621/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316621"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316649/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a541f8ff-b62d-5e66-a809-6d0299be5a9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316649/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "091f1f95-cef9-59b7-b7f9-1415cc9f5aff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316649/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbdfc33-1e58-5242-8633-fda746b517e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316649/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-f