answer-field/choices ["q-316649/field-4/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316649" :question/id #uuid "a501a88c-c742-55d1-9428-8cda49f09e51" :question/math-academy-id "q-316649" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =5(x-(-5))(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ 5({x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+4x+20) & = \\\\ 5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316649/field-1" "q-316649/field-2" "q-316649/field-3" "q-316649/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316649"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316704/field-1/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "201c6278-7349-5fcd-8d3d-50191307ca04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316704/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b12deaa4-cb34-525a-8ae8-02dd21b65c52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316704/field-1/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51d